{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/797705-2e-should-pcs-have-custom-kuruth-triggers","id":797705,"title":"[2E] Should PCs Have Custom Kuruth Triggers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-01T00:37:20-08:00","id":797705,"title":"[2E] Should PCs Have Custom Kuruth Triggers?","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> Checking out the big sidebar on page 103 on Triggers it says that each Werewolf has a set of Triggers that just apply to them. Is there anywhere that gives guidelines on what these could or should be? At what levels of Harmony would these custom Triggers apply? Or are they like the general ones that always apply?<br /> <br /> Edit: While I'm here, what Toxicity would be suitable for a Werewolf sleeping a night in a house slowly filling with Carbon Monoxide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 01-01-2016, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T02:00:56-08:00","id":797719,"title":"","content":"The custom triggers refers to the trio of passive, common and specific. They give a few different examples, like being triggered by 'The Other' or the Moon. The general triggers, those that trigger for all werewolves, is in the lower right. I think the 'sidebar' does a good job of explaining what new ones would be like, especially when coupled with the example triggers.<br /> <br /> At which Harmony they matter is on page 105, and I would generally stick to that chart. I could see a merit or something allowing for variance, but not a trigger itself.<br /> <br /> Some homebrewed triggers were posted shortly after the book came out, you can see them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433833-some-new-kuruth-triggers\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> Sorry, no idea about the carbon monoxide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-01-2016, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T06:31:46-08:00","id":797775,"title":"","content":"Ah so I'm just misunderstading what the sidebar is telling me, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T14:12:53-08:00","id":797969,"title":"","content":"Carbon Monoxide I'd treat via suffocation rules rather than Toxicity. It's preventing them from breathing as opposed to a drug or alcohol. The totem might well notice the pack in danger as well if it's near should it feel its connection with them waning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T14:14:39-08:00","id":797971,"title":"","content":"I'd probably treat it as a low-level extreme environment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T15:41:49-08:00","id":798002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nickpire84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/797705-2e-should-pcs-have-custom-kuruth-triggers?p=797969#post797969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carbon Monoxide I'd treat via suffocation rules rather than Toxicity. It's preventing them from breathing as opposed to a drug or alcohol. The totem might well notice the pack in danger as well if it's near should it feel its connection with them waning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it sense that prior to the effects taking place though? The way CO poisoning works is that it forms carboxyhaemoglobin and until you have enough of that built up in your blood stream it won't cause the suffocating effects but once it has started suffocating you then you're in pretty serious trouble because getting out into clean air doesn't fix the carboxyhaemoglobin problem. Though I guess the healing of Werewolves might fix it.<br /> <br /> There's the Drowning Condition in Beast (which interestingly does nothing to a Werewolf due to healing 1B so quickly...so I'd probably fiddle with that to make it meaningful because I'm fairly sure Uratha can drown). Are there other rules for suffocating/drowning? What happens when an Uratha runs out of air?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T16:30:19-08:00","id":798016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/797705-2e-should-pcs-have-custom-kuruth-triggers?p=798002#post798002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would it sense that prior to the effects taking place though? The way CO poisoning works is that it forms carboxyhaemoglobin and until you have enough of that built up in your blood stream it won't cause the suffocating effects but once it has started suffocating you then you're in pretty serious trouble because getting out into clean air doesn't fix the carboxyhaemoglobin problem. Though I guess the healing of Werewolves might fix it.<br /> <br /> There's the Drowning Condition in Beast (which interestingly does nothing to a Werewolf due to healing 1B so quickly...so I'd probably fiddle with that to make it meaningful because I'm fairly sure Uratha can drown). Are there other rules for suffocating/drowning? What happens when an Uratha runs out of air?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Suffocation in first edition happened after failing to hold your breath, where you started taking one lethal per turn that couldn't be regenerated until you had access to air. That seems a bit much, now, and I'd probably allow for their healing of lethal, since it's magical in nature.<br /> <br /> I don't know if a totem would automatically sense whether or not all members of a pack are in trouble, some might not even care about the extended pack, or even the werewolves if they had been dishonoring their ban. If it was a spirit of protection, prophecy or air I could see it getting wind of what's happening before damage starts accruing. Otherwise I'd wait until the damage started popping up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-01-2016, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T00:40:42-08:00","id":798151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/797705-2e-should-pcs-have-custom-kuruth-triggers?p=798016#post798016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Suffocation in first edition happened after failing to hold your breath, where you started taking one lethal per turn that couldn't be regenerated until you had access to air. That seems a bit much, now, and I'd probably allow for their healing of lethal, since it's magical in nature.<br /> <br /> I don't know if a totem would automatically sense whether or not all members of a pack are in trouble, some might not even care about the extended pack, or even the werewolves if they had been dishonoring their ban. If it was a spirit of protection, prophecy or air I could see it getting wind of what's happening before damage starts accruing. Otherwise I'd wait until the damage started popping up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably go with the Drowning Condition from Beast (1B per turn) once they've run out of breath (after minutes equal to Stamina, probably less if they're doing heavy physical exertion, more if they've a swimming specialty) and no healing it until they've access to air again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T16:06:32-08:00","id":799847,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression that werewolves still needed to breath. I don't think regeneration would prevent suffocation but that could be the 1.0 holdover in my mind. As for the actual mechanics, suffocation was just my best guess for how to handle it. I do think their regeneration could purge the toxins if they got fresh air but ultimately, being a storytelling game, I'd say go with what's dramatic and streamlined rather than worry strictly about realism. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T16:57:50-08:00","id":799862,"title":"","content":"While they do, normally, still need to breath, I was suggesting their regeneration could heal the cells killed via suffocation once things hit Lethal, because healing Lethal damage is a magical thing and magic doesn't really need oxygen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T01:17:19-08:00","id":800379,"title":"","content":"Regeneration treating the Uratha of the consequences of CO poisoning sounds fine, it's like any toxin. Regeneration doesn't creates spontaneous oxigen in one's lungs, tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T05:32:07-08:00","id":800528,"title":"","content":"I would treat CO poisoning as a DoT that increases in potency based on how long you've been in it. I'd research how long it generally takes for it to apply in real life and then factor that by Stamina somehow and maybe give werewolves some extra time.<br /> <br /> However, once you're unconscious from CO, you're probably totally screwed. If you do manage to fall unconscious, I'd say you're CO poisoned, causing further &quot;suffocation&quot; even if moved to fresh air, until you get hyperoxygenated air applied. How exactly this would work is probably mechanically way too complicated to bother, but those are the narrative principles I'd work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T08:49:39-08:00","id":800605,"title":"","content":"CO Poisoning can actually be pretty quick if the concentrations are high enough. 3200ppm is death in 30 minutes, 12000 is unconscious in 2-3 breaths and death in minutes. Someone quietly opening a canister of it in front of your sleeping face could probably kill you before you'd even wake up to know it. Though I imagine wolf senses would warn you if someone was <i>that</i> close anyway even if you were asleep.<br /> <br /> According to this <a href=\"http://www2.gi.alaska.edu/ScienceForum/ASF5/588.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www2.gi.alaska.edu/ScienceForum/ASF5/588.html</a><br /> <br /> A wood fire in a chimney is about 5000ppm and car exhaust without a catalytic converter is about 7000ppm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}